{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_wjmfkxqao52h3vhn3ja6fq27zabsqcktvhkxx3i5jc4psrsyzvia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass, and the Rust translation needed **no fixes** — a result I validated by mutation testing rather than trusting the green run.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is a single 199-line file exporting exactly one symbol: `int dataentry(int mode, int param1, int param2, int param3)`. Everything else (`find_entry`, `process_name`, `calculate_lookup`, `create_entries`, `modify_entries`, `lookup_table`) is `static`, so `dataentry` is the entire public surface, composing all five internal levels.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` on both `.so`s: C exports 1 symbol (`dataentry`), Rust exports the same 1. Symbol diff empty; no C source was left untranslated (all 7 C entities have Rust counterparts, none stubbed). |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 18 rows — every `return NULL`/`return -1`/rejecting `return 0`/`result = -N`/range check in the C — plus 8 generic boundaries (G1–G8). |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 34 rows over the axes the C actually branches on: `mode` ∈ {1,2,3,default}, `count` selection (`param1 > 0 ? param1 : 5/3`), target-index shape (first/last/middle/one-past/negative/wrapping), multiplier shape (0/1/negative/overflowing), all 12 lookup cells, `param3` extremes, and count shapes from 1 to 2 000 000 up to allocation failure. |\n\n## Phases B/C/D — results\n\n- **46 tests** (34 Phase B + 12 Phase C), both `.so`s loaded via `libloading` and called only through their exported `dataentry` — the Rust `#[no_mangle]` wrapper is under test. Randomized, fixed-seed inputs per row; ~150k differential calls.\n- **Feature combos:** Cargo.toml declares no `[features]`, so the powerset is `{∅}`. `run_all_features.sh` derives this mechanically from Cargo.toml (so it still works if features are added), and runs check