ic boundaries (G1–G8). |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 34 rows over the axes the C actually branches on: `mode` ∈ {1,2,3,default}, `count` selection (`param1 > 0 ? param1 : 5/3`), target-index shape (first/last/middle/one-past/negative/wrapping), multiplier shape (0/1/negative/overflowing), all 12 lookup cells, `param3` extremes, and count shapes from 1 to 2 000 000 up to allocation failure. |\n\n## Phases B/C/D — results\n\n- **46 tests** (34 Phase B + 12 Phase C), both `.so`s loaded via `libloading` and called only through their exported `dataentry` — the Rust `#[no_mangle]` wrapper is under test. Randomized, fixed-seed inputs per row; ~150k differential calls.\n- **Feature combos:** Cargo.toml declares no `[features]`, so the powerset is `{∅}`. `run_all_features.sh` derives this mechanically from Cargo.toml (so it still works if features are added), and runs check + build + test + symbol parity for both `--no-default-features` and the default build.\n- Also re-verified in the **debug profile** (overflow checks on) and against the C oracle rebuilt at **-O0/-O2/-O3** — this pins the `wrapping_*` choices for the four signed-overflow sites, where gcc's UB latitude could otherwise diverge.\n\n## The part worth your attention\n\nA suite that passes first try is weak evidence, so I injected 15 deliberate bugs into `src/lib.rs`. **12 were caught** (wrong sentinels, wrong default counts, `find_entry` end-pointer off-by-one, wrong multipliers, inverted `process_name` guard, `param3` added on zero total, `param1`↔`param2` swap, and both mode-3 bound relaxations — those last two abort the harness on the out-of-bounds table index, which my first detector missed until I checked exit codes rather than the failure list).\n\nThe 3 survivors are **provably unobservable** through the only exported entry point, and I documented why in `CONFIGS.md` rather than papering over them:\n- `100.wrapping_add(param2)` → `saturating_add`: both wrapped and saturated ids miss every generated id (a hit needs `count ≈ 2³¹`, which fails to allocate first).\n- Removing the allocator's `isize::MAX` guard: unreachable, since `count ∈ 1..=INT_MAX` ⇒ `nbytes ≤ 85 GiB`, and the negative-`count` path is dead.\n- `\"Entry_\"` → `\"entry_\"`: entry names are only copied into `dataentry`'s local `buffer`, which never reaches the return value.\n\nTwo notes on the setup: `cargo test` alone does **not** produce the `cdylib`, so the runner does an explicit `cargo build` for the matching profile first (the harness panics with that instruction if the `.so` is absent). And `c_src/` is untouched — md5sums unchanged; the only addition is the `c_src/build/` directory the task's own build command creates.","ttft_ms":2981,"ttft_stream_ms":2806,"time_to_request_ms":37,"type":"result","duration_ms":933590,"uuid":"c74c5e9e-4289-48bf-87e2-6b1f6f517cef"}
